    <briefdescription>
<para>Drogon filter that validates the Bearer token and identifies the requester. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Runs last in the SECURE filter chain, after rate limiting and timing (see INSECURE/SECURE in <ref refid="common_8hpp" kindref="compound">basic/common.hpp</ref>). It rejects malformed/missing Authorization headers and invalid tokens with a JSON 401; a <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref> from the validator becomes a retryable JSON 503 with Retry-After: 1. On success it inserts &quot;clientID&quot; and &quot;clientGroup&quot; request attributes that downstream controllers read to build a <ref refid="structRequester" kindref="compound">Requester</ref> for permission checks, then continues the chain. When DatabaseConfig::async is set, validation runs in a drogon::Task coroutine and the callbacks are moved into the coroutine frame so they outlive every suspension. <simplesect kind="note"><para>All routes that consume the identity attributes must include this filter (SECURE). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
